External tree for compiling routines from external sources, including routines
from:

  * the HSL2002 library: MA41 (unsymmetric solver, MA57 symmetric solver
    and EA23 (eigenvector). The targets in the root Makefile are:

         make libhsl

  * the HSL library current, such as updated versions of MA41 and MA57,
    where the last now includes scaling of the matrix and metis renumbering.
    The targets in the root Makefile are:

         make libhsl2

    replaces libhsl, including newer versions of MA41 and MA57

         make libhsl3

    includes libhsl2, AMG (hsl_mi20) and iterative solvers.

  * Sparskit2. The target in the root Makefile is sparskit2:

         make sparskit2

  * Numerical Recipes. The target in the root Makefile is nr.

         make nr

Notes:

  - The MA57 routine from HSL current requires a link to the MeTiS-4 library.
    The MeTiS package can be obtained from
        http://glaros.dtc.umn.edu/gkhome/metis/metis/download.
    Adjust Mdefs.mk according to the directions given in the comments.
    Provided you have a license for MA57, you can ask for a modified MA57 that
    works with MeTiS-5 by sending an email to m.a.hulsen@tue.nl.

  - If you don't want to link with MeTiS, compile the fakemetis routine. The
    target in the root Makefile is fakemetis:

      make hslfakemetis

  - The routines are NOT part of the tfem distribution and needs to be
    obtained separately, most needing some kind of license:

    1) The HSL routines/packages can be obtained free of charge by academics
       for research and teaching purposes. See the website: http://hsl.rl.ac.uk/

    2) The Sparskit2 routines can be obtained from Saad's website:
         http://www-users.cs.umn.edu/~saad/software/SPARSKIT
       and the license is LGPL.

    3) The numerical recipes routines need to be purchased, either as part of
       a book or purchased separately.

  - In order to avoid mixing old and new routines of HSL, the target libhsl2
    includes a "make libhslclean", removing the existing solver library
    completely. Also libhsl3 depends on libhsl2 and therefore completely
    removes the existing solver library.

  - It is recommended to clean the complete external tree at once using

      make externalclean

    instead of cleaning individual packages. The reason is that cleaning an
    individual package will also remove the complete solver library, leaving
    other compiled packages "hanging", unable to build them again. 

  - If you want to go back to libhsl from libhsl2 it is recommended to do a
    complete external tree clean:

      make externalclean

    then build libhsl

      make libhsl

    and rebuild non-HSL external packages again, if needed.






